{
  "id": "12_long_program",
  "description": "Synthetic three-week, three-day plan from an online coach who sends a detailed but practical training note.",
  "tags": [
    "mixed",
    "long_program",
    "coaching_notes"
  ],
  "text": "Week 1 — starting point for the next three weeks.\nAdd a rep where the range allows; add a little weight only when all reps stay clean.\nIf sleep or work gets rough, repeat the previous load. No need to make up missed sets.\nWarm up with a few easy sets on the first lift. They do not count toward the work below.\nAfter the first lift, use the listed rest as a guide and take longer if your breathing has not settled.\nWeek 2: one extra set on most lifts at the same weights; deadlift goes a bit heavier for fewer reps.\nWeek 3: keep the added load on the main lifts, then stop each set with the same form you used in week one.\nMessage me the top set and any joint discomfort; soreness is fine, sharp pain is a stop signal.\nDay 1 – Full Body A\nbench press 3x12/10/8 — Keep your shoulder blades set and touch the lower chest.\n\n\n\nRDL 4×6-8 — خلي البار قريب من رجلك وادفع الحوض لورا.\n\n\n\nlat pull 3 x 8-10 RPE 7-8 — Pull your elbows toward your ribs.\n\n\n\nsquats 4x6-8 2 in reserve — انزل بثبات وخلي ركبتك مع اتجاه صوابعك.\n\n\n\nhip thrust 3×8-10 حتى قرب الفشل\n\n\nAfter the last working set, write down the load and how many clean reps were left.\nDay 2 – Full Body B\nincline DB press 4 x 8-10\n\n\nDB row 3x8-10\nGive your grip a minute to recover before rows; keep the torso quiet.\n\n\nUse the same seat setting next time so we can compare reps fairly.\nleg ext 3×12-15 RIR 1-2\n\n\nface pulls 3 x 12-15 RPE 8\nThe cable should stay taut at the start; step closer if the stack lifts early.\n\n\nTake a few minutes before the next session if the legs are still heavy.\nleg press 4x8-10 RPE 7-8\nKeep the sled range the same across sets; shorten it only if the pelvis starts to roll.\n\n\nDay 3 – Full Body C\nDB lateral raise 3×8-12\n\n\nFor the last set, match the earlier range instead of chasing a heavier dumbbell.\ndeadlift 4 x 4-6\nRest until you can brace properly again; the deadlift is not a conditioning set.\n\n\nleg curl 3x10-12\n\n\nIf the hamstrings cramp, lower the load and keep the hips pressed down.\nab roller 3×6-8 @RIR2\n\n\nBreathe out as the wheel moves away; stop before your lower back dips.\ntricep pushdown 3 x 10-12 RIR 1-2\nWeek 2 note: the extra set is the progress, so keep the week 1 weights.\nWeek 3 note: hold the new load and finish with two clean reps in reserve.\nWeek 2\nDay 1 – Full Body A\nbench press 4x8-10 — 2 min rest\nRDL 4×6-8 — راحة ٢ د\nlat pull 4 x 8-10 RPE 8\nsquats 4x5 2 in reserve\nhip thrust 4×8-10 — 60-90 sec\nDay 2 – Full Body B\nincline DB press 4x8-10\nDB row 4x8-10 — اسحب ناحية الحوض\nleg ext 3×12-15 — R: 2'\nface pulls 3 x 15-20 RPE 8\nleg press 4x10-12 — راحة ٩٠ ث\nDay 3 – Full Body C\nDB lateral raise 4×12-15\ndeadlift 4 x 4-5 — rest 2 min\nleg curl 3x10-12\nab roller 3×8-10 @RIR2\ntricep pushdown 3 x 12-15 RIR 1-2\nWeek 3\nDay 1 – Full Body A\nbench press 2x8 — rest 2 min\nRDL 3×6-8 — راحة ٢ د\nlat pull 2 x 8-10\nsquats 3x5 — ركبتك مع اتجاه صوابعك\nhip thrust 2×8-10\nDay 2 – Full Body B\nincline DB press 3x8-10\nDB row 2x8-10\nleg ext 2×12-15 — R: 2'\nface pulls 2 x 12-15\nleg press 3x8-10 — راحة ٩٠ ث\nDay 3 – Full Body C\nDB lateral raise 2×12-15\ndeadlift 3 x 4 — rest 2 min\nleg curl 2x10-12\nab roller 2×6-8\ntricep pushdown 2 x 10-12\n",
